Subject: [PATCH 0/3] media: ov13b10: Add Device Tree support and active array
 reporting
Cc: Antoine Bernard <zalnir@proton.me>

This series enables the existing OV13B10 driver to match Device Tree
systems and reports the active pixel array area. It is used with the
separate CAMSS and DTS series for the Fairphone 6 ultra-wide camera.

Patch 1 extends ovti,ov08x40.yaml instead of introducing another binding
with the same hardware properties. OV13B10 is a separate compatible, not
a fallback to OV08X40. Its three supplies, populated endpoint and 560 MHz
link frequency are required, while reset remains optional. Both sensors
use the existing one-based two- or four-data-lane constraints, and the
existing OV08X40 requirements are preserved.

Patch 2 adds the OF match table without changing the ACPI match path.
Patch 3 implements CROP_BOUNDS and CROP_DEFAULT for the documented
4208x3120 active area. Per-mode CROP and NATIVE_SIZE are deliberately
left unimplemented rather than publishing unverified geometry.

Antoine Bernard previously submitted OV13B10 Device Tree support for the
Xiaomi Pad 6. The shared binding follows the review request on that work:
https://lore.kernel.org/r/10d6863d-7c66-47ad-a683-251f2a40af66@kernel.org/
Antoine is copied here to coordinate the overlapping binding/OF support.
The three-regulator support by Arun T is already in the upstream base
and is not reimplemented by this series.

Host-side checks of the revision prepared on 2026-09-06 included ARM64
Clang W=1 driver builds with OF enabled, both with and without ACPI,
focused binding checks, both compiled examples, and 66 positive/negative
schema fixtures. Earlier temporary Milos 7.2 boot tests exercised the
sensor's six modes on FP6; the refreshed upstream base has not itself
been boot-tested. Full V4L2 API compliance and image-quality calibration
are not claimed by this enablement series.

Thanks to Jorijn van der Graaf for the suggestion reflected in patch 3.

